<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Polaris adaptive launcher icon (Android 8.0 / API 26+).

    Without this XML, modern launchers treat `mipmap/ic_launcher.png`
    as a "legacy" icon and shrink it inside an auto-generated circular
    frame — Chrome, by contrast, ships an adaptive icon and so fills
    the entire launcher cell. Declaring an <adaptive-icon> here opts
    the icon out of that legacy treatment.

    Foreground: PNG sourced from `assets/icons/polaris-icon-circle-1024.png`
    — a circular cyan disc with the compass design baked in and
    transparent corners. We chose a raster PNG over a vector drawable
    because the artwork is fixed and easier to iterate on outside the
    codebase (Figma/Photoshop), and an opaque circle composites cleanly
    onto whatever launcher mask shape the user has.

    Background: matching cyan gradient (see ic_launcher_background.xml).
    Only ever visible through the foreground's transparent corners —
    e.g. when the launcher mask is a squircle or rounded-square, those
    corners need a fill that reads as a continuation of the cyan disc.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
